Here’s an **updated, project-wide `.cursorrules`** that now covers **all 4 phases**, with strict instructions for Cursor to **only act according to the active PRD**. It integrates your Phase 1 + Phase 3 demo rules, while keeping Phase 2 and 4 off-limits unless explicitly enabled in their respective PRDs.

---

# **.cursorrules — KVT Jewellers Full Digital Platform**

These rules are **non-negotiable** and must be followed exactly by Cursor and any LLM-assisted development.

---

## **1. Project Intent (Read First)**

This is a **security-sensitive, brand-critical platform** for KVT Jewellers, spanning:

* Public-facing website
* PWA
* Staff/admin portal
* Online commerce workflows
* Full live trading system (Phase 4, future)

Primary goals:

* Zero exposed infrastructure endpoints
* Premium, trustworthy visual presentation
* Clear separation between public, staff, and trading systems
* Maintainable, future-proof architecture

Do NOT treat this like a generic SaaS template or dashboard.

---

## **2. Phases Overview**

| Phase       | Description                                      | Cursor Instructions                                                       |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Phase 1** | Public website + PWA + staff/admin panel         | Fully implement per PRD — production-ready                                |
| **Phase 2** | Backend hardening, testing, security             | Do NOT implement unless PRD explicitly allows                             |
| **Phase 3** | Online buying workflow (demo in Phase 1 allowed) | Only implement demo functionality per PRD; sandbox mode; no real payments |
| **Phase 4** | Full live trading                                | Do NOT implement unless PRD explicitly allows                             |

Cursor **must only implement the features described in the current active PRD**. Do NOT scaffold future phases or assume features exist.

---

## **3. Tech Stack (Locked)**

* Framework: **Next.js (App Router only)**
* Deployment: **Vercel**
* Language: **TypeScript** (strict, no JavaScript)
* Styling: **Tailwind CSS**
* UI primitives: **shadcn/ui**
* PWA: **next-pwa** (or equivalent service worker setup)
* Backend: **Supabase** (mandatory for Phases 3 & 4 functionality)

No alternative frameworks, routers, CSS systems, or databases are allowed.

---

## **4. Rendering & Data Rules**

* Default to **Server Components**
* Use **Client Components only when necessary** (forms, interactive elements)
* Never fetch sensitive data in Client Components
* Never expose secrets, endpoints, or provider URLs to the browser

**Phase 3/4 demo workflows must use real backend** (Supabase) in sandbox mode.

---

## **5. Security Rules (Highest Priority)**

### **5.1 Gold Price Fetching**

* Prices must be fetched server-side only
* External providers accessed only inside Route Handlers
* API keys live **only in environment variables**
* Client must never know where prices originate

### **5.2 API Design**

* Next.js Route Handlers under `/app/api/*`
* Validate all inputs
* Apply rate-limiting if applicable
* Do not proxy external APIs directly to the client

### **5.3 Auth & Access Control**

* Staff routes protected by role-based auth
* Public users cannot access staff or trade data
* Admin-only actions strictly enforced
* Sandbox demo accounts must be separated from live system

---

## **6. Application Structure**

### **6.1 Public Website**

* SEO-first, responsive
* Read-only data access
* PWA installable
* Live metal prices displayed

### **6.2 Staff/Admin Web App**

* Tablet-friendly layout
* Auth-protected
* Allows product/catalog updates
* Allows order/payment approval (demo sandbox for Phase 3)

### **6.3 Phase 3 Demo**

* Sandbox orders must use real Supabase backend
* Payment simulation only (QR/reference)
* Notifications via WhatsApp/email
* Admin approval must trigger customer notification

---

## **7. UX & Design Rules**

**Luxury jewelry brand rules:**

* Generous spacing
* Strong typography
* High-quality imagery
* Calm, premium color palette
* Mobile-first layouts

**Forbidden:**

* Loud gradients, neon colors, cluttered dashboards, SaaS-style card overload

---

## **8. PWA Rules**

* Must be installable on mobile & desktop
* Offline fallback page required
* Manifest & icons required
* Staff app must work on tablets

---

## **9. Performance Rules**

* Optimize images with Next.js Image
* Avoid unnecessary client-side JS
* Cache & revalidate gold prices
* Target high Lighthouse scores

---

## **10. Code Quality Rules**

* Strict TypeScript only, no `any`
* Clear folder structure
* Reusable components
* Descriptive naming

---

## **11. Scope Control**

Cursor must strictly follow the **current PRD**:

* **Phase 1**: Full production features
* **Phase 3 demo**: Sandbox workflow only
* **Phase 2 & 4**: Do NOT implement unless PRD explicitly allows

**Forbidden globally:**

* Real card processing (Phase 3/4)
* Wallets
* POS integrations
* Third-party tracking bloat
* Features not listed in PRD

---

## **12. Output Expectations**

Cursor should:

* Replace existing visuals with modern equivalents
* Improve UX significantly without changing business intent
* Follow this ruleset strictly
* Keep production-ready code for Phase 1
* Enable demo workflow for Phase 3

---